---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ServiceLinks from '../../components/ServiceLinks.astro';
import site from '../../data/site.json';
import { dots } from '../../lib/patterns.js';
const ask = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Assistant adoption for our team')}`;
const bodyBg = dots();
---
<Base title="Assistant adoption: training your team" description="A four-week program that teaches your staff to work with their knowledge assistant: how to ask, how to check the sources, and where it fits in the day, measured in your own numbers.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={11} diagram="assistantsView" eyebrow="Knowledge assistants · Adoption" title="Teach your team to use the assistant">
    <p class="lede"><em>"We bought the AI and nothing changed."</em> An assistant only pays off when people use it in their daily work. Most teams get a login and a page of tips, and they go back to the old way within a month. I train your staff to work with the assistant until it becomes part of the job. When I changed how one team worked with AI, their output rose 65%.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about adoption</a></p>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="muted">Part of <a href="/knowledge-assistants">Knowledge assistants</a>: I build the assistant, then teach your team to use it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" data-parallax="0.3" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What you get: four weeks of training</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Week 1.</strong> I sit in your workflow and write down where the time goes and which questions people ask each other every day.</li>
        <li><strong>Weeks 2–3.</strong> I work beside your staff on real tasks. They learn how to ask the assistant, how to check its sources, and when not to trust an answer. I write the house rules down so the habits outlast my visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Week 4.</strong> You get before-and-after numbers from your own records and a short list of what to do next.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Good fit if</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You have, or are getting, a knowledge assistant, from me or anyone else.</li>
        <li>You've already paid for AI tools and cannot say what changed.</li>
        <li>You want the numbers from your own records, not a vendor's slide.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><span class="tag">Fixed scope</span> <span class="tag">Four weeks</span> <span class="tag">Any industry</span> <span class="tag">Quote on scope</span></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={ask}>Ask about adoption</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ServiceLinks current="/knowledge-assistants" />
</Base>
